msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Use this page to upload a workflow, run it, and get its result. The example workflow optimizes and simulates a Qiskit circuit. It simulates the circuit on classical hardware, so it does not use QPU time.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Utilise cette page pour téléverser un workflow, l'exécuter et obtenir son résultat. Le workflow d'exemple optimise et simule un circuit Qiskit. Il simule le circuit sur du matériel classique, il n'utilise donc pas de temps QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin, [install the client package and authenticate](/guides/install-managed-workflows).\n"
msgstr "Avant de commencer, [installe le paquet client et authentifie-toi](/guides/install-managed-workflows).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Use AI skills (optional)\">\n"
"To deploy your own code with help from an AI assistant, use the AI skills in the [Qiskit Function templates repository](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Utiliser les compétences IA (facultatif)\">\n"
"Pour déployer ton propre code avec l'aide d'un assistant IA, utilise les compétences IA du [dépôt de modèles Qiskit Function](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write a workflow {#write-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Écrire un workflow {#write-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the folder structure {#create-the-folder-structure}"
msgstr "Créer la structure de dossiers {#create-the-folder-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow is a folder of Python files with one entrypoint file. A managed workflow uploads everything in the folder, up to 50 MB, and runs the entrypoint as a script. Because a workflow uploads the whole folder, keep your local files, such as `deploy.ipynb`, outside the folder. Create the following layout:\n"
msgstr "Un workflow géré est un dossier de fichiers Python avec un fichier de point d'entrée. Un workflow géré téléverse tout le contenu du dossier, jusqu'à 50 Mo, et exécute le point d'entrée comme un script. Comme un workflow téléverse tout le dossier, garde tes fichiers locaux, comme `deploy.ipynb`, en dehors du dossier. Crée l'arborescence suivante :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the hello world entrypoint {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"
msgstr "Écrire le point d'entrée hello world {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint reads a circuit, optimizes and simulates it, and saves the counts and two-qubit depth. Save the following code as `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"
msgstr "Le point d'entrée lit un circuit, l'optimise et le simule, puis enregistre les comptages et la profondeur à deux qubits. Enregistre le code suivant sous `source_files/hello_world.py` :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you read this page as a notebook, the code cell for `hello_world.py` starts with the `%%writefile` [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile). When you run this cell, it saves the code to the file instead of running the code.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Si tu lis cette page sous forme de notebook, la cellule de code de `hello_world.py` commence par la [commande magique](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile) `%%writefile`. Lorsque tu exécutes cette cellule, elle enregistre le code dans le fichier au lieu de l'exécuter.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint uses three functions from `qiskit_serverless`:\n"
msgstr "Le point d'entrée utilise trois fonctions de `qiskit_serverless` :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_arguments()` returns the keyword arguments that you pass to `run()`, as a dictionary. Each value must be JSON-serializable, or an object that the client can encode, such as a `QuantumCircuit`. Encoded objects arrive as the same objects that you passed.\n"
msgstr "`get_arguments()` renvoie sous forme de dictionnaire les arguments nommés que tu passes à `run()`. Chaque valeur doit être sérialisable en JSON, ou être un objet que le client peut encoder, comme un `QuantumCircuit`. Les objets encodés arrivent sous la forme des mêmes objets que ceux que tu as passés.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` sets the detailed status `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, which you can see while the job runs. See [Report progress with update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"
msgstr "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` définit le statut détaillé `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, que tu peux voir pendant l'exécution du job. Consulte [Signaler la progression avec update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`save_result()` stores a JSON-serializable value that you read later with `job.result()`. The workflow returns the counts as a dictionary and the two-qubit depth of the optimized circuit as an integer.\n"
msgstr "`save_result()` stocke une valeur sérialisable en JSON que tu lis ensuite avec `job.result()`. Le workflow renvoie les comptages sous forme de dictionnaire et la profondeur à deux qubits du circuit optimisé sous forme d'entier.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output, such as the two-qubit depth, goes to the job's logs. To add timestamps and log levels, use the `logging` module. See [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"
msgstr "Tout ce que le workflow écrit sur la sortie standard, comme la profondeur à deux qubits, va dans les logs du job. Pour ajouter des horodatages et des niveaux de log, utilise le module `logging`. Consulte [Écrire des logs et gérer les erreurs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Téléverser le workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In your local notebook, run the following code from the `hello_world_project` folder. The code connects with your saved account, defines the workflow, and uploads it. `entrypoint` is the file that the workflow runs, and `working_dir` is the folder that you upload:\n"
msgstr "Dans ton notebook local, exécute le code suivant depuis le dossier `hello_world_project`. Le code se connecte avec ton compte enregistré, définit le workflow et le téléverse. `entrypoint` est le fichier que le workflow exécute, et `working_dir` est le dossier que tu téléverses :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the workflow with inputs {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"
msgstr "Exécuter le workflow avec des entrées {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct a three-qubit GHZ circuit to pass to `hello_world` as an input:\n"
msgstr "Construis un circuit GHZ à trois qubits à passer à `hello_world` comme entrée :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run `hello_world` with the circuit and the number of shots as keyword arguments. The argument names match the keys that the entrypoint reads with `get_arguments()`:\n"
msgstr "Exécute `hello_world` avec le circuit et le nombre de shots comme arguments nommés. Les noms des arguments correspondent aux clés que le point d'entrée lit avec `get_arguments()` :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`run()` returns a `Job` after the workflow queues the job. It does not wait for the job to run. The job continues in the cloud after you close your Python session. To find it again later, list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "`run()` renvoie un `Job` une fois que le workflow a mis le job en file d'attente. Elle n'attend pas que le job s'exécute. Le job continue dans le cloud après la fermeture de ta session Python. Pour le retrouver plus tard, liste tes jobs récents avec `client.jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: add the web UI for job history when it is available. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the status, result, and logs {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"
msgstr "Obtenir le statut, le résultat et les logs {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
msgstr "Juste après l'appel à `run()`, le statut est généralement `QUEUED` :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The status changes from `QUEUED` to `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING`, and then `DONE`.\n"
msgstr "Le statut passe de `QUEUED` à `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING`, puis `DONE`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to `save_result()`:\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` attend la fin du job, puis renvoie la valeur que le workflow a passée à `save_result()` :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can read the logs while the job runs. The workflow uploads new lines about every 15 seconds. The logs include the line that the workflow printed:\n"
msgstr "Tu peux lire les logs pendant l'exécution du job. Le workflow téléverse de nouvelles lignes environ toutes les 15 secondes. Les logs incluent la ligne que le workflow a affichée :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the workflow {#update-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Mettre à jour le workflow {#update-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To change a workflow, edit its files and call `upload()` again with the same `title`. The new upload replaces the earlier one, and jobs that already started are not affected.\n"
msgstr "Pour modifier un workflow, édite ses fichiers et appelle à nouveau `upload()` avec le même `title`. Le nouveau téléversement remplace le précédent, et les jobs déjà démarrés ne sont pas affectés.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fields such as `arguments_schema` and `sizes_map` keep their stored values when you omit them from the new upload.\n"
msgstr "Les champs comme `arguments_schema` et `sizes_map` conservent leurs valeurs enregistrées lorsque tu les omets dans le nouveau téléversement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Prochaines étapes {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Define inputs and outputs](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) to learn which argument and result types a workflow supports.\n"
"- [Declare dependencies](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) to use more Python packages in your workflow.\n"
"- [Run quantum jobs from a workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) to run your circuits on a QPU, report each stage, and track the QPU jobs.\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to learn all job statuses, debug a failed job, and find a job later.\n"
"- To start from working code, deploy one of the [Qiskit Function templates](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), or adapt a template for your own workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommandations\">\n"
"- [Définis les entrées et les sorties](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) pour savoir quels types d'arguments et de résultats un workflow prend en charge.\n"
"- [Déclare les dépendances](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) pour utiliser davantage de paquets Python dans ton workflow.\n"
"- [Exécute des jobs quantiques depuis un workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) pour exécuter tes circuits sur un QPU, signaler chaque étape et suivre les jobs QPU.\n"
"- [Exécute un workflow géré](/guides/run-managed-workflow) pour connaître tous les statuts de job, déboguer un job en échec et retrouver un job plus tard.\n"
"- Pour partir d'un code qui fonctionne, déploie l'un des [modèles Qiskit Function](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), ou adapte un modèle à ton propre workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
